What Is TPU Paint Protection Film?
TPU means thermoplastic polyurethane. It is a durable, flexible polymer and the industry standard for premium paint protection film. TPU stretches without cracking, stays clear, and often has a self-healing top coat that clears light scratches with the help of heat.
What TPU Film Offers
Solid resistance to rock chips and road debris
Self-healing for light swirls and scratches
Clear finish with little yellowing
Good fit on curves and edges
Up to 10 years of life with proper care
What Is TPH Paint Protection Film?
TPH means thermoplastic hybrid. It is a blended-polymer film positioned as an entry-level choice. It gives basic protection from light scratches and road dirt, but it is generally less flexible and less durable than TPU. Some sellers call the material thermoplastic polyolefin, so ask your installer for the exact specification.
What TPH Film Offers
A lower price tag
Basic protection from light debris
Lower elasticity, so curves are harder to wrap
Limited or no self-healing
A shorter lifespan, and it may yellow with time
