The Difference Between TPH and TPU Explained
In short, the difference is material quality. TPU is a flexible, self-healing polyurethane film that is made for long-term protection. TPH is a hybrid film that is cheaper, yet gives basic protection, lower elasticity, and a shorter life. TPU is a good match for most owners, whereas TPH is a good match for tight budgets.
TPU vs TPH PPF for Cars: Which Wins?
TPU is the better choice for most cars. It lasts longer, heals light scratches, and holds its clarity. TPH can still work if budget is your top priority or you plan to sell your car before long.
TPU is a good fit if you:
Want long-term car paint protection
Own a new, luxury, or high-value car
Drive often on highways or gravel roads
TPH is a good fit if you:
Need the lowest cost to start
Plan to sell the car soon
Only want basic protection
How to Choose the Right PPF Material for Your Car
Ask about the material. Confirm whether the film is TPU or TPH, and which brand.
Think about how long you'll own the car. Long ownership favors TPU.
Check the warranty. A longer warranty is a sign of a more durable film.
Pick a skilled installer. Even the best film fails when it is applied badly.
